<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Walmu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Walmu was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilusa">Wilusa</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in the late 13th century BCE. He is known from the so-called Milawata letter, written by a Hittite king, probably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tudhaliya-iv">Tudhaliya IV</a>, which records that Walmu had been driven out of Wilusa and that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> intended to restore him as their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. The episode reflects the struggle for influence in western Anatolia that involved the Mycenaean king of Ahhiyawa.</p></div>
